      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#include <omp.h>\n#endif\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    // Read matrix using scanf for speed (as original)\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> mat(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i][j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Build integral image (prefix sum) of size (n+1)x(n+1)\n    std::vector<std::vector<long long>> pref(n + 1, std::vector<long long>(n + 1, 0));\n\n    // First pass: row-wise prefix sums\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row_sum += mat[i][j];\n            pref[i + 1][j + 1] = row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Second pass: column-wise accumulation to get full 2D prefix sums\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n        long long col_sum = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            col_sum += pref[i + 1][j + 1];\n            pref[i + 1][j + 1] = col_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Search all SxS submatrices using integral image\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    #pragma omp parallel for collapse(2) reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(guided)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n            long long sum = pref[i + s][j + s] - pref[i][j + s] - pref[i + s][j] + pref[i][j];\n            if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", static_cast<int>(mxSum));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Use integral image with OpenMP work sharing during construction (row-wise and column-wise prefix sums using static scheduling) and collapse(2) reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(guided) on the search phase to demonstrate adaptive guided scheduling for load balancing. This demonstrates OpenMP work sharing via parallel for directives, reductions via max reduction, explicit scheduling control through static/guided schedules, and thread granularity via collapsed loops.",
  "notes": "Changed only the search loop's schedule from runtime to guided. The prefix sum construction retains static scheduling as before. Guided scheduling adaptively assigns larger chunks early and smaller later, potentially improving load balance for irregular iteration costs (though here iterations are uniform). This is a new variant not previously tested in own_role_history.",
